LOW-01: Missing Security Headers on Main Application
========================================
Severity: LOW
CVSS 4.0: 2.6 (AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N)
CVSS 3.1: 2.6 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N)

Description:
The main application lacks security headers (noted as out of scope per policy, but documented for completeness):
- No Content-Security-Policy
- No X-Frame-Options
- No X-Content-Type-Options
- No Referrer-Policy
- No Permissions-Policy

Note: Policy explicitly lists "Missing HTTP security headers" as out of scope.

========================================
LOW-02: Cookie Configuration Issues
========================================
Severity: LOW
CVSS 4.0: 2.6 (AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N)
CVSS 3.1: 2.6 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N)

Description:
Cookies set by the application lack secure flags:
- cookiebot cookies missing Secure and SameSite attributes
- Webflow session cookies may lack HttpOnly flag

Evidence:
Set-Cookie: cookiebot=...; path=/; domain=.cronometer.com (missing Secure, SameSite)

Impact:
- Cookie theft via MITM on non-HTTPS (unlikely as site enforces HTTPS)
- CSRF risk if SameSite not set to Lax/Strict

Remediation:
- Add Secure flag to all cookies
- Add SameSite=Lax (or Strict) to session cookies
- Add HttpOnly to session cookies

